  "verbalization": "Alitretinoin, a retinoid derivative, is shown to have a target relationship with NCI-H1436 through multiple pathways, all of which converge on a common intermediate compound: 3-[2-[4-[5-[2-(2,3-Dihydroxyphenyl)ethyl]-2-hydroxyphenoxy]phenyl]ethyl]benzene-1,2-diol. This compound is identified as the target of alitretinoin in three distinct pathways, each linking alitretinoin to NCI-H1436 through a shared mechanism. The evidence suggests that alitretinoin exerts its biological effect by inhibiting the activity of this compound, which in turn interacts with NCI-H1436. The consistent presence of this intermediate across different target relationships implies a potential mechanism of action involving the inhibition of a specific enzymatic or biochemical pathway that is critical for NCI-H1436 function. The integration of these pathways supports the hypothesis that alitretinoin may act as a modulator of NCI-H1436, though further validation is needed to confirm the exact nature of the interaction and its relevance to disease.",
